  {
   "name": "SHOW DRIVES.DMO",
   "id": "show_drives",
   "kind": "demo",
   "reject": [
    "\\?[a-z0-9 ]+error"
   ],
   "notes": "Works with the emulated 1541 (true drive): lists drive 8, then '1 Drive connected.' The earlier ?DEVICE NOT PRESENT ERROR IN 230 came from VICE's virtual IEC device (-busdevice8), which returned ST=-125. Timing-fragile (11 Nov): the program tests ST=-128 exactly, and device 16 sometimes answers -125 (not present + timeout bits) depending on when RETURN is pressed; then it ends with ?DEVICE NOT PRESENT ERROR IN 230. With RETURN delayed 0-5 frames, the released CRT fails at +3 and the EasyFlash CRT at +0. The scenario presses RETURN 1 frame after the start screen is stable, which passes on both (reports/1.4-easyflash-crt.md)",
   "steps": [
    {
     "stable": 120,
     "cap": "start"
    },
    {
     "frames": 1
    },
    {
     "type": "\r"
    },
    {
     "stable": 120,
     "max": 4000,
     "cap": "drive8"
    },
    {
     "type": " "
    },
    {
     "end": 1,
     "max": 6000,
     "expect": [
      "1 drive connected"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
